mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Biochemistry is a crucial foundational and compulsory course for medical students.It explores the chemical composition, structure, and chemical principles of life activities in living organisms at the molecular level, elucidating the essence of life processes. Building upon chemistry, biology, and other disciplines, the course content encompasses the structure and function of biological macromolecules (proteins, enzymes, nucleic acids); the metabolism of carbohydrates, lipids, and amino acids along with energy metabolism; and the transmission and regulation of genetic information. It helps students master fundamental theories and techniques for application in the medical field.&nbsp;</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
